# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Node / Vite
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.vite

# Editor
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code local state (any nesting level, not just repo root)
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# CCIMP local custom config (per-machine layout / session / avatar /
# TTS state; the app writes these alongside the regular config).
**/.ccimp.custom.config.json
# Stale pre-rebrand local custom config (old `cctts` name); never commit.
**/.cctts.custom.config.json
# Schema-migration backups: when the backend bumps schema_version, the
# previous file is renamed with a `.vN.M.bak` suffix (sometimes with a
# trailing timestamp, e.g. `.bak.1778262818`).
**/.ccimp.custom.config.json.*.bak*

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
.aider*

# Local release-staging output (workflow assembles this in CI; ignore if
# you experiment with `npm run tauri build` followed by manual staging).
staging/
download/
release-notes.md
ccimp-portable-*.zip

# Local build/run logs (transient, e.g. tauri-dev.log, release-build.log)
/*.log
